## a discarded first attempt at M5, kept because it is the lesson
The first M5 inserted a return above 'if not un:' and left that branch with no body -> IndentationError.
The battery then exited rc=1 with NO named red cell (red=[]). rc=1 with no named cell is a CRASHED battery,
not a caught mutation; reading it as 'caught' would have been the same error family as treating a backgrounded
job's exit as its result. M5 was rewritten to the real defect shape (report_net quoting a bare point while
unresolved episodes exist) and then went red on RT6 as intended.
